00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.000
Live it up!

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.210
Nice work!

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.830
Today's surprise concert sure was intense!
Why, you!<b></b>

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.460
Today's surprise concert sure was intense!

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:18.710
EIKO was great too, but Azalea's final song was lit!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.290
The vid of their concert got a crazy number of likes.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.330
Huh, probably fake accounts.
I mean, they're with Key Time.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.460
Oh, if it isn't Karasawa from Key Time.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.500
I did not expect you would join us this evening.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.290
I'm tying up loose ends.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.040
Well, would you care for a drink?

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:38.880
No.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.290
Perhaps a different kind of liquor?

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.920
I don't accept booze from the enemy.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.000
Satisfied?

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.750
You've made an enemy of Key Time, you know.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.830
An enemy?
Goodness, no.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:52.710
That said, isn't it true that one cannot know
the outcome of a war without fighting it?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:57.670
I know countless others who've
acted pretentious like that only to disappear.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:02.790
When you say "disappeared," would that
include one's past self?

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:07.080
In your younger days,
without joining up with a major agency,

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.880
you and your buddies made music together.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.920
But one day, one of the band members betrayed-

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.130
Shut up!

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:18.540
<b>I am the</b>

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:18.540
<b>mastermind</b>

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:17.750
It is enough to just tell the stories of the winners.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.670
And that's why you wanted to make
those girls a success at any cost.

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.460
You wanted to make them winners.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.750
So that they do not end up as you did.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:29.500
The one who believes in their talent most of all...

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.420
is none other than you, Karasawa.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.880
Do not throw around the word "talent."

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.000
This is a business.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.670
Those girls indeed have talent.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:45.460
However, they failed to convey its brilliance.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.670
It's an all-too-familiar story in music.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.460
Depending solely on how it's promoted,
good stuff ends up getting buried.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:57.290
But at today's concert,
their own music was widely appreciated.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.830
I suspect they could make it without my help now.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.580
Karasawa, that isn't what you promised us, now is it?

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.960
You said you'd have us doing a dome tour, didn't you?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.170
Ichika!

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.420
You girls! How long have...

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:19.580
I got a message from the tactician guy saying,
"Seeing this will be of interest."

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.830
I see you used to play in this band, Karasawa.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.250
You look super cool!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.790
So you used to be a rocker, huh?

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:30.250
<b>I am the</b>

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:30.250
<b>mastermind</b>

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.580
Karasawa!

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:36.250
I apologize for stepping out of line today!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:42.250
That said, that is the Azalea
we really want to be, after all!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.040
Performing live today was a real blast!

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:48.830
More than dancing, I feel at home playing the drums.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:55.130
Will you please take on this reborn Azalea
and produce us one more time?

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.330
You girls...

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.920
But be warned, music is a business.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.880
My stance on that is firm.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.080
Okay!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.750
I see, very well, then.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:16.960
Um, but, try to be gentler if you can.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:19.250
I mean, you can be quite pushy, Karasawa.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:21.670
Also, those outfits are out from now on!

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:27.000
I'll turn you girls into stars!

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.670
Yes, sir, please and thank you!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.670
<i>Nanamin, you did it!</i>

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.460
<b>Congrats on making it</b>

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.460
<b>to Summer Sonia!</b>

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.040
<i>I'm...</i>

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.880
<i>really going to perform at Summer Sonia.</i>

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.500
<i>Kongming has brought me this far.</i>

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:01.630
I shall be your tactician.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.170
Tactician, huh?

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:12.750
Kongming!

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.210
So this is where you were.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:18.580
Well, well, hello, Eiko.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.790
Sure you want to be up here?

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.880
The party has just begun.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.040
Yeah...

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:24.830
But what are YOU doing up here?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.580
I got an urge for some fresh air,
and I'm having a celebratory drink.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.580
Ah, makes sense.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.460
It really is packed on the dance floor.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:37.290
And all present are people who were
captivated by your song.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:42.540
Once again, congratulations on
securing a spot at Summer Sonia.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:45.040
I didn't do that all on my own!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.330
It's thanks to everything you did for me.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.210
Thank you, Kongming.

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:53.790
I came to tell you that.

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.000
In the past,

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:03.920
I employed stratagems in which I was willing to
make any sacrifice for the sake of victory.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.670
The result was the taking of many lives.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.880
<b>Stratagem</b>

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.880
<b>of</b>

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.880
<b>Alienation</b>

